IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- APPLICATION FOR A RETIREMENT PENSION, AND THE ANNUAL
-- ADJUSTMENT OF BENEFITS (regulations 61 and 62; 60, 60.1 and 60.2 are repealed).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 612 to 628.
--
-- Regulation 61: what an applicant for a retirement pension files with the application.
-- Regulation 62: how the annual adjustment under section 45(2) of the Act is rounded. The product of the basic
-- monthly amount and the ratio is rounded to the nearest cent by looking at the third digit after the decimal point
-- (5 or more rounds up); the ratio itself is first expressed to three digits by looking at the fourth.
-- ROUND of the language rounds half to even, so the rounding is written out: FLOOR (x TIMES 100 PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100.

§ `Part V -- Application for a retirement pension and annual adjustment (regulations 61 and 62)`

§§ `Regulation 61 -- the statement an applicant for a retirement pension files`

-- src:613 | 61 An applicant for a retirement pension shall, in addition to any other information or material that these Regulations require him to file or furnish, file with the Minister a statement of the amount of his contributory salary and wages and of his contributory self-employed earnings
-- src:614 | (a) for the year in which the application is made; and
-- src:615 | (b) if the Minister so requires, for the year preceding the year in which the application is made.
@ref Reg 61 (src:613-615)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant for a retirement pension` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the year in which the application is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 61 — the applicant must file a statement of contributory salary and wages and contributory self-employed earnings for a year`
    `the person is an applicant for a retirement pension`
    `the year in which the application is made`
    `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made`
    year MEANS
    `the person is an applicant for a retirement pension`
        AND (    year EQUALS `the year in which the application is made`
              OR (    year EQUALS (`the year in which the application is made` MINUS 1)
                  AND `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made`))

@ref Reg 61 (src:613-615)
GIVEN `the year in which the application is made` IS A NUMBER
      `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`reg 61 — the years for which the applicant must file a statement`
    `the year in which the application is made`
    `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made` MEANS
    `the year in which the application is made` FOLLOWED BY
        (IF `the Minister requires a statement for the year preceding the year in which the application is made`
         THEN LIST (`the year in which the application is made` MINUS 1)
         ELSE EMPTY)

§§ `Regulation 62 -- the annual adjustment of benefits`

-- 62(2): a product with a fractional part of three or more digits is rounded to the nearest cent; the third digit decides.
-- src:618 | 62 (1) When the basic monthly amount of a benefit is adjusted annually pursuant to subsection 45(2) of the Act,
-- src:619 | (a) the product obtained by multiplying the amount referred to in paragraph 45(2)(a) of the Act by the ratio referred to in paragraph 45(2)(b) thereof shall be adjusted to the nearest cent in accordance with subsection (2); and
-- src:620 | (b) any quotient obtained from the ratio referred to in paragraph 45(2)(b) of the Act shall be expressed as a decimal fraction in accordance with subsection (3).
-- src:621 | (2) Where the product referred to in paragraph (1)(a) contains a fractional part of a dollar represented by three or more digits, and
-- src:622 | (a) where the third digit is less than five, the third and subsequent digits shall be dropped; and
-- src:623 | (b) where the third digit is five or greater than five, the second digit shall be increased by one and the third and subsequent digits shall be dropped.
@ref Reg 62(2) (src:621-623)
GIVEN product IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 62(2) — a product adjusted to the nearest cent` product MEANS
    FLOOR ((product TIMES 100) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 100

-- 62(3): the ratio is expressed to four digits and rounded to three by the fourth digit (fork F-62).
-- src:624 | (3) Where the quotient referred to in paragraph (1)(b) contains a fraction that is less than one, that fraction shall be expressed as a decimal fraction of four digits after the decimal point, and
-- src:625 | (a) where the fourth digit after the decimal point is less than five, the third digit after the decimal point shall remain unchanged and the fourth digit shall be dropped; and
-- src:626 | (b) where the fourth digit after the decimal point is five or greater than five, the third digit after the decimal point shall be increased by one and the fourth digit shall be dropped.
@ref Reg 62(3) (src:624-626)
GIVEN ratio IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 62(3) — a ratio expressed as a decimal fraction` ratio MEANS
    FLOOR ((ratio TIMES 1000) PLUS 0.5) DIVIDED BY 1000

@ref Reg 62(1) (src:618-620)
GIVEN `the amount referred to in paragraph 45(2)(a) of the Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 45(2)(a) (piece cp3)
      `the ratio referred to in paragraph 45(2)(b) of the Act` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 45(2)(b) (piece cp3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 62(1) — the basic monthly amount of a benefit after the annual adjustment`
    `the amount referred to in paragraph 45(2)(a) of the Act`
    `the ratio referred to in paragraph 45(2)(b) of the Act` MEANS
    `reg 62(2) — a product adjusted to the nearest cent`
        (`the amount referred to in paragraph 45(2)(a) of the Act`
         TIMES (`reg 62(3) — a ratio expressed as a decimal fraction` `the ratio referred to in paragraph 45(2)(b) of the Act`))
